      "text": "Given the problem:\n- \\( A + B + C + D = 36 \\)\n- \\( A + 2 = B - 2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2 \\)\n\nFirst, let's denote the common value by \\( k \\). Thus, we have:\n\\[\nA + 2 = k\n\\]\n\\[\nB - 2 = k\n\\]\n\\[\nC \\times 2 = k\n\\]\n\\[\nD \\div 2 = k\n\\]\n\nFrom these equations, we can express \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) in terms of \\( k \\):\n\\[\nA = k - 2\n\\]\n\\[\nB = k + 2\n\\]\n\\[\nC = \\frac{k}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nD = 2k\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute these expressions into the sum equation \\( A + B + C + D = 36 \\):\n\\[\n(k - 2) + (k + 2) + \\left(\\frac{k}{2}\\right) + 2k = 36\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\nk - 2 + k + 2 + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36\n\\]\n\\[\n4k + \\frac{k}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate the fraction, multiply every term by 2:\n\\[\n8k + k = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n9k = 72\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\( k \\):\n\\[\nk = \\frac{72}{9} = 8\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( k = 8 \\) back into the expressions for \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\):\n\\[\nA = k - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nB = k + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\nC = \\frac{k}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nD = 2k = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\):\n\\[\nA \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16\n\\]\n\nFirst, multiply \\( 6 \\) and \\( 10 \\):\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply \\( 4 \\) and \\( 16 \\):\n\\[\n4 \\times 16 = 64\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply the results:\n\\[\n60 \\times 64 = 3840\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3840}\n\\]",
